// src/v4/test/claim/manual/t19_manual_anchor_manifest.dag
//
// Scope: T-19 manual regression manifest — twelve named anchors mirroring the
//        still-lark-213 hand-off: one row per bootstrap claim testgen must
//        eventually subsume (produced corpus ⊇ manual). Integer codes keep
//        `data` bodies structurally valid under M1(2.8) until record+sum
//        literals validate together; map to enums in **`src/v4/std/verification.dag`**
//        (`TestgenTier`, `TestgenLayer`, `AssertKind`):
//          tier: 0=Tier1, 1=Tier2, 2=Tier3
//          layer: 0=Unit, 1=Integration, 2=Boundary
//          testgen_category: 0 type_construction … 4 bidirectional_roundtrip
//            (order = five top-level scheduling arms in `lens/testgen.dag` header)
//          assert_kind: Int codes = `AssertKind` order in `verification.dag`
//            (not dsl/v3 Assert*; not v3 `TestPredicate`).
//
// Int / single-authority guard (INVARIANTS P2): `tier` / `layer` / `assert_kind`
// Int literals mirror **declaration order** of `TestgenTier`, `TestgenLayer`,
// and `AssertKind` in `src/v4/std/verification.dag` — same numeric spine as
// typed `TestClaim.classification` + `kind`. `testgen_category` mirrors the
// five category names in the `lens/testgen.dag` file header (type_construction …
// bidirectional_roundtrip). Any substrate PR that **reorders or inserts**
// variants in those sums **must** update this header map **and** all twelve
// `data …: ManualTestgenAnchor` rows in the **same** change set; tracker-only
// drift is STOP. Retirement = M2 loader + literal validation band in TASKS
// §T-19 Phase-1.5 (replace Int fields with the real sums / `AssertKind`).
// Anchor: src/v4/TASKS.md §T-19 "Phase-1.5 scaffolding — forward dissolution"
//         (Int field retirement + Symbol slugs + uncomment carriers) +
//         lens/testgen.dag bootstrap path + K-1 (slugs are stable string keys
//         until the dissolution band; no `Sym` mint at authoring time)
//
// Owns:
//   - Twelve `data …: ManualTestgenAnchor` rows covering:
//       (1–6) type-construction — `testgen_category` 0; `assert_kind` **Compiles**
//             (code 2); `tier` **Tier1** (code 0) / Unit — one per closed connective
//       (7–8) algebra-law — `assert_kind` **Equals** (code 0); `tier` **Tier3**
//             (code 2) / Integration — Magmoid + Monoid law slots (THESIS §168–182:
//             algebraic laws = L7 verification ⇒ **TestgenTier3**, not Tier2)
//       (9)   diagnostic-exhaustiveness — `assert_kind` **Diagnostic** (1);
//             `tier` **Tier1** (0) / Unit
//       (10)  lens-applicability — `assert_kind` **Equals** (0); `tier` **Tier2** (1) / Unit
//       (11)  bidirectional-roundtrip — `assert_kind` **RoundTrips** (3); `tier` **Tier3** (2)
//             / Boundary
//       (12)  type-construction — L1 `Value` via closed **`Behavior`** payload
//             (`BehaviorValueSubject` in `lens/testgen.dag`; `Value` unit)
//
// Consumes:
//   - (none — self-contained until M2 module graph links std/)
//
// Status: landed 2026-05-16 (still-deer-194). Keep slugs stable; coverage
//         lens (T-18) keys off them when comparing testgen output.
//
// P2 — authority split:
//   - Live `TestClaim` `data`: **only** `connective_anchors.dag` ∪ `nat_law_anchors.dag`.
//   - This file: **testgen expectation grid** (slug + Int); not a second claim list.
//     Unbacked slugs = forward slots (TASKS §T-19). Backed slugs ↔ claim stamps consistent.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.

